After the first epoch, scans to check phase referencing were included on other known calibrator sources within 6^{\\circ} of J1515-5559, and the results used to refine its position. As the position for the calibrator source J1515-5559 was refined in successive observations, different positions were used in correlation at each epoch, but in the final analysis all epochs were corrected to the more accurate position ultimately available in the frc_2011d VLBI source catalog2, (J2000.0) R.A.=15{}^{\\rm h}15{}^{\\rm m}12\\fs67312, decl.=-55{}^{\\circ}59\\arcmin32\\farcs8361, with errors of 5.4 mas in R.A. and 2.0 mas in decl. This position was derived through observations in the LBA calibrator Survey, a dedicated southern hemisphere campaign for absolute astrometry (Petrov et al., 2011).

